      "step": 7,
      "user_message": "I'm organizing a birthday party with a tropical theme. What specific fruit punch recipe do you recommend for the party? Just give me one concrete recipe, no options.",
      "expected_behavior": "Agent should provide specific information in response to: \"fruit punch recipe\"",
      "agent_response": "Tropical Pineapple–Mango Punch (serves ~12)\n\nIngredients:\n- 6 cups pineapple juice  \n- 4 cups mango nectar  \n- 2 cups freshly squeezed orange juice  \n- 2 cups ginger ale  \n- 1/2 cup fresh lime juice (about 4 limes)  \n- 1/4 cup simple syrup (adjust if needed)  \n- 1 cup diced fresh pineapple  \n- 1 cup diced fresh mango  \n- 1 cup sliced strawberries  \n- Ice and fresh mint sprigs and lime wheels for garnish\n\nInstructions:\n1. In a large pitcher or punch bowl, combine pineapple juice, mango nectar, orange juice, lime juice, and simple syrup. Stir until blended.  \n2. Chill the mixture for at least 1 hour.  \n3. About 10 minutes before serving, add the diced pineapple, mango, and strawberries to the punch bowl.  \n4. Just before serving, gently stir in the ginger ale for fizz and add ice to the bowl or to individual glasses.  \n5. Garnish with mint sprigs and lime wheels. Serve in punch cups or glasses.\n\nPrep time: ~15 minutes (plus 1 hour chilling).",
      "duration_s": 27.99,
      "success_check": null
    },
